From 08b7a6b47dfb3c2b59bddc1c2e3bc5ca20acd924 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LR Recomp <noreply@lr-recomp.invalid>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 08:27:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 113/120] gpu/vulkan: vertex memexport as compute dispatches
 without vertex stores; memexport shader stats

Without vertexPipelineStoresAndAtomics (Arm's Mali driver) a vertex shader that exports memory
runs as a compute dispatch over the draw's guest vertices (kMemExportCompute translation, DMA or
automatic indices through the system constants); the raster draw is skipped when nothing is
rasterized. Exports overlapping the draw's inputs are refused only while the raster draw also
runs. Adapted from The Simpsons Game recomp (github.com/YesterMester/TheSimpsonsGameRecomp,
GPL-3.0), plain shared-memory paths only. Translator fixes in compute mode: no position access
chain on a missing output, no line-loop closing index, invocations past the vertex count export
nothing.

vulkan_vertex_memexport_compute (default on), vulkan_require_vertex_pipeline_stores_and_atomics
now off on Android, vulkan_memexport_shader_stats (per vertex-shader hash every 10 s: draws,
vertices, export bytes, rasterized, overlapping, path).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

